    "productsHeading": "Compare patio cover types",
    "productsLead": "Compare the main patio cover types, then get a quick rough quote in chat before booking a free on-site measurement.",
    "seoHeading": "Custom patio covers and sunrooms for Vancouver-area homes.",
    "seoBody": "Backed by a team with 10+ years of combined experience and hundreds of completed projects across the Lower Mainland, LoomiHome helps homeowners compare aluminum patio covers, glass patio covers, skyline combo designs, and sunroom options with fast rough pricing in about a minute. Start with a ballpark estimate first, then book a free on-site measurement when you're ready.",
    "seoServiceArea": "Serving Vancouver, Burnaby, Richmond, Surrey, Delta, Coquitlam, Langley, North Vancouver, West Vancouver, New Westminster, Maple Ridge, Pitt Meadows, and the wider Lower Mainland.",
    "faqTitle": "Quick answers",
    "faqItems": [
      {
        "q": "How fast can I get a rough estimate?",
        "a": "Pretty quick — jump into the chat, tell us your city and roughly how big the space is, and we’ll give you a ballpark number in about a minute. No need to wait around for someone to call you back first."
      },
      {
        "q": "What types of patio covers do you offer?",
        "a": "We work with aluminum covers, glass covers, skyline-style combo (glass plus V-panel), and sunrooms. Same team, same process — pick what fits your home and we’ll walk you through it."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do you serve Vancouver and nearby cities?",
        "a": "We’re all over the Lower Mainland day to day — Vancouver, Burnaby, Richmond, Surrey, Delta, Coquitlam, and the surrounding neighbourhoods. If you’re close by, chances are we’ve been on a job near you."
      },
      {
        "q": "Can I get pricing before booking a measurement?",
        "a": "That’s the idea. Chat first for a rough range so you know if you’re in the ballpark. If it makes sense, we’ll book a free on-site visit to measure properly and nail down final pricing — only when you’re ready."
      },
      {
        "q": "What’s the difference between glass and aluminum patio covers?",
        "a": "Aluminum roofs are usually the practical rain-first choice. Glass lets in more light and looks premium — often at a higher price point. We’ll ballpark both so you can decide what fits."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do patio covers help with rain in Vancouver?",
        "a": "A properly built cover keeps your patio drier and more usable through the wet months. Material and drainage matter — we talk through that in chat and confirm on site."
      },
      {
        "q": "How much does a patio cover usually cost?",
        "a": "Size and product type move the number a lot. The chat estimate is the fastest way to get a range for your patio; our cost guide page walks through what typically drives price."
      },
      {
        "q": "Are sunrooms more expensive than patio covers?",
        "a": "Usually yes — more glass, enclosure, and insulation. We can rough-quote both if you’re comparing."
      },
      {
        "q": "Do I need a permit for a patio cover?",
        "a": "It depends on your municipality and design. Check with your city — we align installation details to what they require. See our permit guide for general homeowner notes."
      },
      {
        "q": "How long does installation usually take?",
        "a": "Every job differs. After we measure, we’ll give a realistic schedule. Our timeline guide explains typical phases from estimate to completion."
      }
    ]
  },
